    <description>LingoGeek translates whole documents on your own machine. No account, no character limit,
and nothing is uploaded.

* Word documents, with headings, lists, tables, headers and footers kept in place
* PDFs, read as text and written out as an editable Word document
* SRT and VTT subtitles, with every cue number and timestamp copied through exactly
* Markdown and plain text
* Around 100 language pairs from the openly licensed Argos and OPUS-MT collections
* A pack downloads once, 40 to 80 MB, and works offline from then on
* Your original is never overwritten: the translation is written as a new file beside it

Free at home and at work. Everything it needs is inside the installer.</description>
    <summary>Free offline document translator for Windows: Word, PDF, subtitles and text</summary>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/techygeekshome/LingoGeek/releases/tag/v1.0.0</releaseNotes>
